WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.600
In 1977, one radio signal looked so unusual that an astronomer wrote one word: Wow.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:14.200
It arrived near a frequency researchers considered promising for interstellar communication and lasted seventy-two seconds.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:21.633
Its strength rose and fell as the telescope beam crossed the source, making ordinary local interference less convincing.

00:00:21.633 --> 00:00:27.500
But later searches never verified the same signal again, and no confirmed transmission has explained it.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:34.167
The honest answer is not aliens. It is one strong unexplained candidate that left no repeatable proof.
